## Purpose

Build one authoritative quantum/frontier closure ledger over current `main` and every open ORION-Q/QG/quantum issue. Separate mathematical results, implementation receipts, physical claims, resource-accounting claims, transfer claims, and novelty authority.

## Required outputs

- issue/result/status census;
- theorem and countermodel map;
- Q-series versus physical-quantum namespace audit;
- typed transfer bridges into ORION V1;
- full oracle/compiler/verification resource accounting;
- exact positive/negative/`CANNOT_CHECK` disposition for every open issue;
- duplicate/obsolete issue map;
- frozen successor jobs only where current evidence is insufficient.

## Claim boundary

Quantum structure may donate quotient-state, syndrome, noncommutation, resource-monotone, tensor/factor, adaptive-measurement, phase-boundary, and recovery mechanisms. It does not grant quantum advantage, physical validity, or novelty without target-native validation and independently governed comparisons.
